~ vitest.config.ts
#order vitest.config.ts
#order test/codeview.test.ts
#order test/lantern-diff-view.test.ts
#order test/lantern-macro-layout.test.ts
#order test/lantern-macro-current.test.ts
#order test/lantern-macro-areas-pr-view.test.ts
#order test/material-file-icons-build.test.ts
#reason test/codeview.test.ts Loading shiki grammars and tokenizing every registered language is heavy by design on a slow runner.
#reason test/lantern-diff-view.test.ts Rendering a few thousand context lines is CPU-heavy and timed out on the hosted runner.
#reason test/lantern-macro-areas-pr-view.test.ts Walking every file of the pull request with the stepper is long by design on a slow runner.
#reason test/lantern-macro-current.test.ts Walking every file of the pull request with the stepper is long by design on a slow runner.
#reason test/lantern-macro-layout.test.ts Laying out the macro graph for every block and system is CPU-heavy on a slow runner.
#reason test/material-file-icons-build.test.ts Each case spawns the build script several times, which outlasts 5 s on a small runner.
#reason vitest.config.ts A 2-vCPU CI runner ran heavy tests past the 5 s default, so CI gets 30 s timeouts and two workers.
#story CI runs the tests on a small runner
#step actor A contributor pushes a branch
#file vitest.config.ts
#step action Starts the test suite on the CI runner
#file vitest.config.ts
#step subject Seven heavy tests
